<title>SINGAPORE: Sime Singapore to sell insurance sector.</title>
<headline>Sime Singapore to sell insurance sector.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sime Singapore Ltd said on Monday it had agreed to sell its general and health insurance business to AXA for a cash consideration of Singapore $57 million.  </p>
<p>The group recently announced it would build a string of service apartments. Its other businesses includes selling BMW cars and packaging.</p>
<p>An analyst with a local firm said he was surprise at the sale as its Malaysian parent, Sime Darby, has a successful insurance joint venture with the AXA group in Malaysia.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't think they need the money but maybe they want to rationalise their business,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
</text>
